WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.434
-It is so good to see you, pal.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.834
-It's good to see you, too.
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.801
Congratulations.
You have a new baby.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.501
-Yes.
-A beautiful, beautiful baby.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:12.734
-Wait till you see this baby.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.334
-Oh, yeah.
This is the newest picture.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.000
This is yesterday.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.067
Look at this.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.167
She's cute.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.501
-Isn't that
the most perfect baby

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:21.501
you ever seen in your life?
-She's really sweet.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.601
And I had a boy first,
and she's a girl.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.868
And it turns out,
they're a little bit easier.

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:28.033
-Yeah, girls a little bit
easier than boys, yeah.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.601
I have to tell you, you know,
I've known you a long time.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:31.901
I love you.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.834
And I watched "Yellowjackets,"
and it's --

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yay!

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.901
Yes.
-100% fresh on Rotten Tomatoes,

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:44.000
by the way.
It is unbelievable.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.133
It is so --
It's so scary.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.000
It's too scary for me.
-It's fun.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.767
My sister says
that when she watches it,

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:52.300
she's just filled with
such a sense of dread.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.901
-It's not even dread.
I don't know.

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.367
It's not dread.
It's like the thing,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.501
the mask with the fur,
a little eye coming out.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:00:59.701
-Yeah.
-That scares me.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.501
-That is scary.
There is some scary stuff.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:03.901
Yeah. The eyeless man
is terrifying.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.367
-Of course it is.
-Terrifying.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:08.167
It's -- It's like things that
you go like, "Oh, this is --"

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.567
It's on a different level.
-Yeah.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.167
-But I will say, also, you're
very funny in it, as well.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.968
-Oh, thanks.
-'Cause I know you're funny.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.467
You have a great sense of humor.
You're a jokester.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.634
But I mean, I've seen --
-I'm not really funny.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:22.634
I've never really been funny
intentionally for work.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.033
-That's true.
But off-camera you're funny.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.734
-Yeah, I'm a goof.
-But you're funny in this thing

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:29.000
when you're throwing the food
and stuff.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.567
Yeah. No, I had a really good
time doing all that stuff.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.834
-Season two, already announced.
Congratulations.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.434
-Yeah. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:37.734
Thanks.
We shoot end of August.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.901
-End of August.
Is it fun?

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:42.467
Do you enjoy it, or are you
scared as much as I'm scared?

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.901
-No, I'm not scared at all.

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:47.167
And, also, my character's
a villain, so, you know,

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.033
I don't have to be afraid
of anything.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.000
-Whoa.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.567
I always kind of --
Yeah, I always wanted to play

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.634
a character like this,
so it's really fun.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:59.901
-Do you follow any of
the fans' theories online?

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:02.100
-I did.
Well, I'm old, so I didn't know

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.667
where to find these fan theories
for quite some time,

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.501
and then one of the younger
people helped me,

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:08.701
so I found them.
-Yes.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.667
-And I think they're
fascinating.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:13.200
It's really interesting.
-I thought it would kind of fun

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.000
maybe if I read some of the fan
theories from the Internet,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.701
and you tell me
what you think of these,

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.934
and if they're true or not.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.033
-Is the baby one on there?
'Cause that's the worst.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.100
-What's the baby one?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.501
-That was the one
I was obsessed with

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.200
and just thought was so insane.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.334
"Do they eat Shauna's baby?"
-What?

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.434
-Right. And I was like,
"Why would we eat the baby?"

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:33.734
And then I thought,
"Well, we are really ashamed --

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.534
Everybody else is, like,
really haunted by what they did,

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:37.934
so maybe we do eat the baby."

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.167
So I had to ask the writers,
I said,

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:40.901
"We don't eat Shauna's baby,
do we?"

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.701
And she said, "No."
-All right, good.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.400
Thank you.
No, do not.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.367
That's good to hear.
We don't want anyone eating...

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.400
[ Applause ]

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.234
All right. You ready?
-Yeah.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:55.534
-Your character, Missy,
is a present-day serial killer.

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:58.200
-Well, I mean, she does --
It's very --

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.467
I mean, she casually
murders somebody,

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:03.734
and she has a bunker ready
for kidnap victims.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:07.300
I mean, that bunker
was ready to go, pretty much.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.901
-Yeah.
So, yeah. So this --

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.767
-I would say that
she's probably done it before.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.501
But I don't know.
Like, all of this is just

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.467
my opinion because
they don't tell me anything.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:19.534
-Okay. So you --
She's done it before -- maybe.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.567
-I think so.
It was really easy.

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:25.334
Casual.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:28.300
-"Jackie is still alive."

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.601
-I don't see how that one is
possible, to tell you the truth.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:34.100
-Okay.
-I don't see how -- no.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.434
I mean, she froze to death.
We saw it.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.767
-I know we did.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:41.334
-I just don't --
-Okay, good.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.367
Not possible.
-I don't think so.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:48.601
-"Misty caused the plane
to crash."

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.868
-I mean, we saw her
in that episode,

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:53.634
and she looked very surprised.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.067
-Mm-hmm.
-Right?

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.534
-Well, as one --
-She looked shocked.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:59.434
-Well, you don't want to look
calm as the plane is crashing.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:01.501
-That's true. That's true.
Could've been a performance.

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.701
-She's not an actor.
-But she seems pretty --

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.901
I mean, she seemed
genuinely shocked.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:08.467
Because she's not an actor.
She's on a plane

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.901
that's going down
with the soccer team.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:14.868
-So she did a bad job
or a good job?

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:18.167
-It was the human reaction
to cover up, but she knew,

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:20.067
maybe that it was
gonna go down?

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.367
-Yeah, I don't know.
-The whole thing is insane.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.634
-Yeah, it's pretty crazy.
-Okay. All right.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.334
So you're saying no.
-I don't think so.

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:28.100
-"Misty has been working under
Lottie and her henchmen

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.834
and henchwomen this whole time."
-Yeah, that's interesting.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:34.701
I think that is possible,
but I don't know.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.334
-It's unbelievable.
-I know. There's a lot --

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.000
They don't tell us anything.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.701
-Okay. But...

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:42.367
Some things you have more
confidence than others.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:43.467
-Yes, that's true.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.367
-Yeah, some things
seem more possible.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:46.934
-Juliette Lewis' character, Nat,

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:48.300
gets kidnapped
at the end of season one.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.601
We all know that.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:52.601
Does Misty have anything to do
with the kidnapping?

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:53.968
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:56.200
-Yeah!
-I heard a strong yes

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.300
from over there.
-Yeah!

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.234
-So when I first
heard this theory,

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.133
my initial instinct is no.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.868
She would never do anything
to hurt Natalie.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.100
But then,
the more I thought about it,

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.834
I was like, "Oh, maybe."

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:10.601
Maybe she did, like, Lenny
and the kitten, you know?

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.100
-Yeah, "Of Mice and Men."
-She wants it so much,

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.868
she's gonna, yeah, crush her.
Yeah, it's possible.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:16.234
-Are you --
Did you know the show

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.367
was gonna be a hit
when you were doing it?

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.467
-No. No.
I mean, I liked it.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:20.868
And I thought the concept
was good,

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.501
and the scripts became
increasingly, like,

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.734
Stephen King-y in tone,
which I was so excited about

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:28.501
because I love Stephen King.
-Fascinating and scary.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.300
-Yeah.
-And "What is gonna happen?"

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.133
But I love the flashbacks.

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:33.801
I love the music, by the way,
is great, too.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.200
-Yeah.
-'Cause you flashback,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.601
you're like, "I was there,
and I listened to that music."

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.734
-I know, I know.
Liz Phair.

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.367
When they sing the Liz Phair
song, I was like --

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:42.434
-Dude, I put it on a playlist
because I'm like,

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:44.234
"Oh, yeah, I love Liz Phair."

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:45.634
All right.
Well, congratulations on that.

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:47.634
Thank you for clearing that up,
or not clearing it up.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:48.901
I love it.
-Not clearing anything up

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:50.334
for anyone.
-I want to talk about

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:54.968
"Monstrous," in theaters, and on
demand, by the way, May 13th.

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:56.968
Another one
with lots of twist and turns.

00:05:56.968 --> 00:06:00.601
-Yeah, it is
a psychological thriller

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:03.267
shot in the sort of tone --

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:06.400
or, the style of, like,
a '50s horror film.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.834
-Yeah.
-And it's about --

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:12.334
Ostensibly, it is about a woman
and her son

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:15.300
in the late 1950s or '60s

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.300
who is escaping
an abusive relationship.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.801
And they're moving
to a new town, new house.

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:21.968
And then when they get
to the house,

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:24.701
all these sort of
supernatural-feeling things

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.000
start to happen.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.501
And the character that I play
devolves over time.

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:30.567
But as she devolves,
you realize that things

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:32.601
are not quite as they seemed.

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:37.367
-No.
And the final twist is...

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:38.834
-It's emotional, also.

00:06:38.834 --> 00:06:40.334
Like for a horror film,
it's very emotional.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.767
-Yeah, it is.
I agree, yeah.

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.567
-And as a parent, it's scary.
-Kind of beautiful and wild.

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:45.667
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.234
Here's Christina Ricci
in "Monstrous."

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:48.501
Take a look at this.

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:50.501
-[ Breathing heavily ]

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.968
Cody, are you okay?

00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:10.033
♪♪

00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:13.100
♪♪

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:17.300
[ Gasps ]

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:19.901
-Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:19.901 --> 00:07:21.133
Christina Ricci.

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:25.501
I did want to mention, too,
as well.

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:29.067
Here's baby Christina Ricci
in "Addams Family" in 1991.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:30.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-With my favorite toy.

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:32.434
-Come on.

00:07:32.434 --> 00:07:35.934
And did you fall in love with
movies when you did this?

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:38.200
-I did.
I think "The Addams Family" --

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.767
One, those movies were
so formative for my career,

00:07:41.767 --> 00:07:44.400
because the first thing I did
that was really successful

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.634
was all about me
being allowed to do something

00:07:46.634 --> 00:07:48.667
that was not conventional,
so it really sort of

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:51.200
shaped everything for me
in so many ways.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.834
And then, also, I remember --

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:54.901
You know, I kind of fell into
being a kid actor.

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:56.200
I hadn't --
I didn't --

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.400
It was brought to me,

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.133
and then I was like,
"Okay, sure. I'll do this."

00:08:00.133 --> 00:08:02.167
But I had always planned on
doing something different.

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:04.868
And then, I remember, I was 13,
and I was walking

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:08.601
on the Paramount lot and
shooting "Addams Family 2."

00:08:08.601 --> 00:08:10.501
And they were shooting
"Coneheads" next door,

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:12.033
and then "Frasier"
was over here.

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.801
And I was like,
"Yeah, you know what?

00:08:13.801 --> 00:08:15.567
I think I, um --
I think I want to do this

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:16.634
for the rest of my life."

00:08:16.634 --> 00:08:17.801
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:08:17.801 --> 00:08:19.033
-You figured it out
right then and there?

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:21.267
-Yeah, it was just such
an incredible experience.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.033
-And now you're filming
"Wednesday."

00:08:23.033 --> 00:08:24.734
-Yeah.
-Which is for what?

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:27.033
What is it gonna air on?
-It's on Netflix.

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:28.167
-Netflix.
-Netflix and it is --

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:29.968
-Tim Burton.
-Yeah, it's Tim Burton.

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:31.334
And it's a new --

00:08:31.334 --> 00:08:35.934
It's young Wednesday,
teenage Wednesday in school.

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:37.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:37.467 --> 00:08:39.567
-Are you playing --
-Jenna Ortega plays Wednesday.

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:41.634
The only thing I can tell you
about my character

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:43.133
is that I do not play Wednesday.

00:08:43.133 --> 00:08:44.434
-Okay.
That's the only thing.

00:08:44.434 --> 00:08:45.567
-It's the only thing
I'm allowed to say.

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.467
-And how is she?
-Amazing.

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:48.767
She's so good.

00:08:48.767 --> 00:08:50.634
So good and so wonderful
to work with,

00:08:50.634 --> 00:08:54.234
and her Wednesday
is, like, really an incredible

00:08:54.234 --> 00:08:55.567
great, modern take.
-I think you'd be a great person

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:58.434
to work opposite,
being a child actor yourself.

00:08:58.434 --> 00:09:00.834
-Well, I always loved working
with adults who have been

00:09:00.834 --> 00:09:03.434
child actors 'cause there's,
like, just an unspoken

00:09:03.434 --> 00:09:06.133
kind of thing we all know.
-Yeah.

00:09:06.133 --> 00:09:08.567
-It's really weird,
but it does work out that way.

00:09:08.567 --> 00:09:10.434
-You're awesome, bud.
Christina Ricci, everybody.

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:13.968
"Monstrous" is in theaters
and on demand May 13th.

